# Serve index.html at the bare "/" without a redirect.
#
# html_handling is "none" (see wrangler.jsonc), which does no path rewriting at all, so
# "/" matches no file on disk and the front door 404s. A 200 here is a rewrite, not a
# redirect: the URL stays "/" and no hop is added. Doing it this way rather than switching
# html_handling keeps every other URL literal, so /field-guide.html is still served as
# itself instead of redirecting to /field-guide.
/    /index.html    200

# Extensionless addresses for the pages, e.g. /press serves press.html (John, 2026-10-02).
# Also 200 rewrites, so the URL people type stays as typed and the site's own links (which
# end in .html) are untouched. One line per page: a NEW PAGE OR BLOG POST NEEDS ITS LINE,
# and tools/check-site.js fails if one is missing. Other cases and a trailing slash
# (/Press, /press/) are handled by worker.js, not here.
